<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex" />
    <title>forge can't be reached · forge</title>
    <Layouts.theme_script />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href={~p"/assets/css/app.css"} />
  </head>
  <body class="bg-bg text-ink">
    <%!-- The page a device keeps and shows when a page load fails. It holds no value from the
          server and no form: the button and the `online` event only reload the address that was
          asked for (`docs/design/ui.md` § The installed app). --%>
    <main id="offline" class="sign-in">
      <div class="sign-in-body">
        <p class="sign-in-wordmark">forge</p>
        <h1 class="offline-title">forge can't be reached</h1>
        <p class="offline-text">
          This device is offline, or the server isn't answering. The page will load as soon as it can.
        </p>
        <.button id="try-again" type="button" variant="secondary">Try again</.button>
      </div>
    </main>
    <script>
      (() => {
        const again = () => location.reload();
        document.getElementById("try-again").addEventListener("click", again);
        window.addEventListener("online", again);
      })();
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
